What you say is largely true, but there are two major exceptions.

First, it is very common for people to be in medical conditions that require
immediate urgent care and/or conditions where transport is dangerous.  Consider
someone who has severe trauma, or requires ACLS (Advanced Cardiac Life Support).
For severe trauma an hour may be too long.  For CPR situations, count the minutes.

This is an interesting twist to the question of how much people value health care.
Since a large chunk of the population lives too far away from the nearest ambulance,
