Subject: Outlawry

I imagine that to be allowed into most locations, from a condo complex
to a city to a geographic region, one would be required to declare
one's PPL.  The location would then have a policy about whether to let
you in, and what new contracts you must sign at the door to get in.  

Forbidding entrance by outlaws might be standard, hence giving outlaws
much less freedom of movement.  Of course there might be locations
that cater to these folks, but they would be exceptions.  

Better yet, I imagine travelers being required to have crime
insurance, which would pay for damages due should the traveler turn
outlaw.  Insurance premiums for previous outlaws would of course be
high.  Nick is of course right that for some people these extra
expenses and restrictions may be worth it for the thrill of a life of
crime.  But they should be a deterrent, none the less, and detererence
is the best we can hope for.

Robin Hanson

