Well, I could start by noting that things like illegal drugs won't be
illegal in a PPL environment, but you do have a point -- which is that
if a strong minority wants crimes to continue they will continue. Look
at drug trading right now, for example. The hope is that in a PPL environment
these things will become scarce. Insurance fraud, for instance, is
suprisingly rare -- this because insurance companies are good at combatting
it and fraudsters have little public support. I doubt that outlaws
would survive well in a PPL environment, but certainly your point is
correct -- no system will work if there is strong dissent against it
by a very large minority. My belief is that such a minority will not arise,
but certainly in the presense of such a group NO system can function
optimally. As an example, I doubt peace is really possible in Bosnia,
for much this reason. (Once enough of the beligerants die off, things
will likely calm down -- but this is more a tribute to evolution than
to Cyrus Vance and Lord Owen.)

